return {
["04:00"]={"Nothing happened, he said wanly. “I waited, and about \003four o’clock\004 she came to the window and stood there for a minute and then turned out the light.”","The Great Gatsby","F. Scott Fitzgerald"},
["04:01"]={"Charlie glanced at the clock. \003Barely past four a.m.\004 at home. Sunday. She’d be up. Probably reading over a cup of coffee before taking a run before church.","Soldier On","Vanessa Rasanen"},
["04:02"]={"I walked up and down the row. No one gave me a second look. Finally I sat down next to a man. He paid no attention. My watch said \0034:02\004. Maybe he was late.","The History of Love","Nicole Krauss"},
["04:03"]={"It’s \0034:03 a.m.\004 on a supremely cold January morning and I’m just getting home. I’ve been out dancing and I’m only half drunk but utterly exhausted.","The Time Traveler’s Wife","Audrey Niffenegger"},
["04:04"]={"\003Four minutes after four!\004 It’s still very early and to get from here to there won’t take me more than 15 minutes, even walking slowly. She told me around five o’clock. Wouldn’t it be better to wait on the corner?","Angel Hill","Cirilo Villaverde"},
["04:05"]={"Leaves were being blown against my window. It was \0034:05 am\004. The moon had shifted in the sky, glaring through a clotted mass of clouds like a candled egg.","We Were the Mulvaneys","Joyce Carol Oates"},
["04:06"]={"Dexter looked at Kate’s note, then her face, then the clock. It was \0034:06 am\004, the night before they would go to the restaurant.","The Expats","Chris Pavone"},
["04:07"]={"\0034:07 am\004. Why am I standing? My shoulders feel cold and I’m shivering. I become aware that I’m standing in the middle of the room. I immediately look at the bedroom door. Closed, with no signs of a break-in. Why did I get up?","Guarding Hanna: A Novel","Miha Mazzini"},
["04:08"]={"It was at \0034:08 a.m.\004 beneath the cool metal of a jungle gym that all Andrew’s dreams came true. He kissed his one true love and swore up and down that it would last forever to this exhausted companion throughout their long trek home.","Dying in the Twilight of Summer","Seth O’Connell"},
["04:09"]={"It was \003nine minutes past four\004. “He’s sitting in the middle of an ultrasonic field and I’m ten minutes late to get him out. Come on!”","The Final Affair: A Man from U.N.C.L.E.","David McDaniel"},
["04:10"]={"I don’t like this waiting, he said.\nShe smiled. “You’d make a terrible PI.”\n“What time is it?”\n“\003Four-ten\004. Fifteen minutes later than the last time you asked.”","Copper River","William Kent Krueger"},
["04:11"]={"The next morning I awaken at exactly \003eleven minutes after four\004, having slept straight through my normal middle-of-the-night insomniac waking at three.","The Stuff of Life","Karen Karbo"},
["04:12"]={"Karen felt the bed move beneath Harry’s weight. Lying on her side she opened her eyes to see digital numbers in the dark, \0034:12\004 in pale green. Behind her Harry continued to move, settling in. She watched the numbers change to 4:13.","Get Shorty","Elmore Leonard"},
["04:13"]={"Karen felt the bed move beneath Harry’s weight. Lying on her side she opened her eyes to see digital numbers in the dark, 4:12 in pale green. Behind her Harry continued to move, settling in. She watched the numbers change to \0034:13\004.","Get Shorty","Elmore Leonard"},
["04:14"]={"At \0034:14 a.m.\004, the two men returned to the Jeep. After the passenger replaced the cans in the back of the Jeep, the driver backed out of the driveway and headed east. The last images found on the film appeared to be flames or smoke.","A Real Nightmare","David H. Swendsen"},
["04:15"]={"Alice wants to warn her that a defect runs in the family, like flat feet or diabetes: they’re all in danger of ending up alone by their own stubborn choice. The ugly kitchen clock says \003four-fifteen\004.","Pigs in Heaven","Barbara Kingsolver"},
["04:16"]={"They pulled into the visitor’s carpark at \003four sixteen\004 am. He knew it was four sixteen because the entrance to the maternity unit sported a digital clock beneath the signage.","Freaks in the City: Book Two of the Freaks Series","Maree Anderson"},
["04:17"]={"He awoke at \0034:17 am\004 in a sweat. He had been dreaming of Africa again, and then the dream had continued in the U.S. when he was a young man. But Inbata had been there, watching him.","The Vile","Douglas Phinney"},
["04:18"]={"I grabbed the alarm clock, threw it on my lap, and slapped the red and black buttons with both hands. The ringing didn’t stop. The telephone! The clock read \003four-eighteen\004. It was dark outside. Four-eighteen a.m. I got out of bed and picked up the receiver. “Hello?”","Hard-Boiled Wonderland and the End of the World","Haruki Murakami"},
["04:19"]={"At \003nineteen minutes past four\004 on the morning of December 27, 2040, her eyes, dark as an Aztec sacrificial knife, flicked open.","Aurora Quest","James Axler"},
["04:20"]={"At each waking he switched on the light and glanced at his bedside clock, hoping to find that dawn was near to breaking. Two-ten, three-forty, \003four-twenty\004.","The Lighthouse","P.D. James"},
["04:21"]={"At \003twenty-one past four\004 I inferred that the initial hostilities had not damaged its works. It was running, and I didn’t know whether to interpret this indifference on the part of Time as a good or bad omen.","The Tin Drum","Günter Grass"},
["04:22"]={"The chairman dialed seven digits and asked to speak to the duty officer. He checked his watch as he waited to be put through. It was \0034:22\004.","Honor Among Thieves","Jeffrey Archer"},
["04:23"]={"\0034:23\004, Monday morning, Iceland Square. A number of people in the vicinity of Bjornsongatan are awakened by loud screams.","Let the Right One In","John Ajvide Lindqvist"},
["04:24"]={"At \00304:24\004 on January 5, 2025, the stars stood still in the sky. In California, the earthquake started with a low-frequency rumble. It wasn’t a sound but a sensation that caused an incomprehensible weakness in the legs, a constriction of the bowels, and panic.","Perfect Circle","Carlos J. Cortes"},
["04:25"]={"As I dressed I glanced at my watch. It was no wonder that no one was stirring. It was \003twenty-five minutes past four\004.","The Adventures of Sherlock Holmes","Sir Arthur Conan Doyle"},
["04:27"]={"And then I heard the school bell in my dream but it wasn’t really a school bell and the pitch went very steep like a trap door opening and I fell and landed in my bed. It was still dark and my alarm clock said \00304:27\004 and I heard the noise again.","The Dead Fathers Club","Matt Haig"},
["04:30"]={"Jonas rolls painfully out of the hammock, his aching lower back stiff and swollen, in desperate need of a chiropractor. He checks his watch. \003Four thirty\004…but is it a.m. or p.m.?","Meg, Primal Waters","Steve Alten"},
["04:31"]={"As Miss Nichol walked along the corridor, she checked her watch. It was \0034:31 A.M.\004 She took the stairs down to the fifth floor and made her way to the nursery.","Sons of Fortune","Jeffrey Archer"},
["04:32"]={"On his first day of kindergarten, Peter Houghton woke up at \0034:32 a.m.\004 He padded into his parents’ room and asked if it was time yet to take the school bus.","Nineteen Minutes","Jodi Picoult"},
["04:34"]={"He was not pleased about being pulled out of his dream. The clock taunted him, saying it was \0034:34 AM\004. He picked up the receiver.","Warrior Monk","Ray Keating"},
["04:35"]={"No manner of exhaustion can keep a child asleep much later than six a.m. on Christmas Day. Colby awoke at \0034:35\004.","Dreams and Shadows","C. Robert Cargill"},
["04:36"]={"At \0034:36\004 that morning, alone in my hotel room, it had been a much better scene. Spencer had blanched, confounded by the inescapable logic of my accusation. A few drops of perspiration had formed on his upper lip. A tiny vein had started to throb in his temple.","The Brass Go-Between","Ross Thomas"},
["04:37"]={"The knock at the door was soft, but it still awoke Stephen. He touched the screen on his smartphone. \0034:37 AM\004","Under the Golden Dome","Ray Keating"},
["04:38"]={"At \0034:38 a.m.\004 as the sun is coming up over Gorley Woods, I hear a strange rustling in the grass beside me. I peer closely but can see nothing.","The Queue","Jonathan Barrow"},
["04:40"]={"I settled into a daily routine. Wake up at \0034:40 am\004, shower, get on the train north by ten after five.","Bossypants","Tina Fey"},
["04:41"]={"At \0034:41\004 Crane’s voice crackled through the walkie-talkie as if he’d read their thoughts of mutiny. “Everyone into the elevator. Now!” Only moments before the call he and C.J. had finished what they hoped would be a successful diversion.","Damaged Goods: A Novel","Roland S. Jefferson"},
["04:42"]={"A large clock above the desks read \00304:42 am\004. He paused to listen. Whatever had happened there, appeared to be over.","Dead City","Matthew Warwick"},
["04:43"]={"The time is \003four forty-three\004 in the mornin an it’s almost light oot there.","Pyschoraag","Suhayl Saadi"},
["04:45"]={"He never found it necessary to phone the Prime Minister, although Mr. Churchill did phone him on one occasion. It was \003four forty-five\004 in the morning when Charlie picked up the receiver on his desk.","As the Crow Flies","Jeffrey Archer"},
["04:46"]={"The phone rang again at \003four-forty-six\004.\n“Hello,” I said.\n“Hello,” came a woman’s voice. “Sorry about the time before. There’s a disturbance in the sound field. Sometimes the sound goes away.”\n“The sound goes away?”\n“Yes,” she said. “The sound field’s slipping. Can you hear me?”","Hard-Boiled Wonderland and the End of the World","Haruki Murakami"},
["04:47"]={"I slept only fitfully after looking online. The phrases I’d read repeated in my head over and over again. When I woke up for what felt like the hundredth time, the Stormtrooper clock beside the bed read \0034:47 am\004.","What She Knew","Gilly MacMillan"},
["04:48"]={"At \0034:48\004 the happy hour when clarity visits warm darkness which soaks my eyes I know no sin","4:48 Psychosis","Sarah Kane"},
["04:49"]={"When Costain left the bridge the brass chromometer in the wheelhouse said \003eleven minutes to five\004. Harkness looked at it and realised vaguely that the gap was still too big.","Gale Force","Elleston Trevor"},
["04:50"]={"Even the hands of his watch and the hands of all the thirteen clocks were frozen. They had all frozen at the same time, on a snowy night, seven years before, and after that it was always \003ten minutes to five\004 in the castle.","The 13 Clocks","James Thurber"},
["04:51"]={"Earlier? It’s \003nine minutes to five a.m.\004 — who would be up this early?\n“Oh, we’re all early risers.”","Gifts of the Magi","Jean Johnson"},
["04:52"]={"If it matters, it’s \003eight minutes to five\004. Don’t get any persecuted ideas that I enjoy being out of bed at this time of night. It makes it legally easier if you invite us in.","Holding the Zero","Gerald Seymour"},
["04:53"]={"It was so quiet in the post office that Trinidad could hear the soft tick of the clock’s second hand every time it moved. It was now \003seven minutes before five\004.","The Silence of Bonaventure Arrow","Rita Leganski"},
["04:54"]={"When the last lid had been placed back on he checked the clock on the wall: \003six minutes to five\004. Just enough time to glance in the other box and see if he could expect the same again.","A Matter of Honor","Jeffrey Archer"},
["04:55"]={"\0034:55\004 — Mank holding phone. Turns to Caddell — “Who is this?”\nCaddell: “Jim.” (shrugs) “I think he’s our man in Cincinnati.”","Fear and Loathing: On the Campaign Trail ’72","Hunter S. Thompson"},
["04:56"]={"Trying to identify the key facts, Ethan was suddenly aware he was looking at the wall clock; it was 7:35.\n“Wait a minute. When did you hear about this?”\nThere was a tiny moment of hesitation. “The first news came in \003just before five\004.”","The Infinite Day","Chris Walley"},
["04:57"]={"One hundred and thirty-one seconds were lost at Elkhart in changing locomotives, and it was \003three minutes to five\004 when big 599, with Dave Luce in the cab, turned her nose toward the dawning day and started for Toledo, 133 miles away.","Careers of Danger and Daring","Cleveland Moffett"},
["04:58"]={"He wants to look death in the face. \003Two minutes to five\004. I took a handkerchief out of my pocket, but John Dawson ordered me to put it back. An Englishman dies with his eyes open. He wants to look death in the face.","Dawn: A Novel","Elie Wiesel"},
["04:59"]={"The captain and his three mates appeared out of the early morning mist at \003one minute to five\004. All four of them were dressed in exactly the same clothes they had been wearing the night before, making Percy wonder if they’d come straight from the Fisherman’s Arms.","The Undiplomatic Diplomat","Jeffrey Archer"},
